# Spider-Man Noir: "Whenever a creature you control attacks alone, put a +1/+1 counter on it. Then surveil X, where X is the number
# of counters on it" (CR 506.5, 122.1, 701.25). "It" is the attacker, not Noir: Aboroth attacks alone while Noir stays home. Aboroth
# already has an age counter and a -1/-1 counter from its cumulative upkeep (CR 702.24a), so with the +1/+1 counter it has three
# counters of three kinds - the +1/+1 and -1/-1 pair is not removed until state-based actions are next checked (CR 704.5q) - and
# Bot1 surveils 3, putting Plains, Mountain and an Island into the graveyard. Noir gets no counter and stays a 4/4.

